Update - I solved the mystery: very low detection probabilities (duh). So my next question is, do low detection probabilities render all model inference meaningless, that is, can I make any reasonable conclusions from my models in spite of this e.g. through model outputs and predictor covariates? Or perhaps there's a way to mitigate this situation altogether, addressing the inflation of predictions in order to obtain reasonable ones (previous posts I've read seem to suggest that there's not much that I can do... crossing my fingers that someone can tell me otherwise!)? Again, thanks in advance for your advice!

